        <head>Singular Death of a Master Plumber.</head>
        <p>Singular Death of a Master Plumber.</p>
        <p>An inquest was conducted at Warrington on Tuesday by Mr S Brighouse, county coroner, re- specting the death of John Molyneux, a master plumber, who resided at 37, Napier-street, and died at 215 that moning as the result of injuries received on Monday.—The Coroner said the case was rather a curious one. The deceased and his two sons were engaged in fixing a pump in a well thirty-nine feet deep in a farm yard at Grappenhall on Monday, when a man, who was hawking lamp- oil.stepped on a plank at the top of the well,eausing the plank to slip, and kno3king a paving tile down the well. The tile fell on deceased's head. Deceased was removed home in a cab and died that day. —John Davies Molyneux, son of the deceased, gave evidence bearing out this statem ant The accident occured at Mr R Broady's farm —A. verdict of " Accidental death" was returned.—Mr J Whitley, of Stockton Heath explained that it was his son who was hawking the lamp oil and he felt the matter very keenly. It appeared that he could not get along the footpath without stepping on the pink. He narrowly escaped falling into the well. Mr Whitley expressed the deepest sympathy with. the relatives of the deceased.</p>
