      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-11-14_WidnesExaminer_art0075" n="art0075">
        <head>WORTH YOUR ATTENTION.</head>
        <p>WORTH YOUR ATTENTION.</p>
        <p>Every person's future 13 ton certain extent in his own hand. Many a future which might have been brilliant hat been darkened by lack of timely preparation to meet the exigencies and changes which occur in every day life. Many a home which might have been gladdened by life and health, and comfort, has been saddened by poverty, illness, and death, in many cases wholly pre- ventable. Neglect now may mean a broken constitution to succumb under the attacks of any exceptional trial. There are, indeed, few that do not feel the system needs recruiting after the trying feeling of lassitude, with others, "not quite up to the mark," " a sort of all over sinkinn feeling," " too weak to do anything about the house," " these recurring headaches," " no appetite for my fool," etc. These, and a dozen others, are common expressions which all point to the urgent need of some good tonic mixture, a reliable medicine of established reputation and of proved virtue. There are several tonic mixture to be hid, but none which have been so uniformly successful at Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bittere ; it has never been known to fail. It's always the same, there can be no mistake about it. The careful preparation and a manipulation of manufacture under the most stringent rules, assures the certainty that Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, The Vegetable Tonic, is always efficacious and genuinely successful in all eases of Indigestion, Weakness, Nervous- ness, Low Spirits, Sleepleasness, Dyspepsia, Liver Com- plaints, Newalgia, and influenza. We claim that Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is • General Benefactor of Suffering Humanity. Hundreds of teatimonials pr 3Ve till!, coming from all CLUMPS of the cernmunitY. Pain is no respect:sir of perverts, he advised, try Gwilyrn Evans' Quinine Bitters, a sovereign remedy for various ail- Monte, for rich and poor alike. When you buy Gwilyrn Evans' Qninine Bit'ere, you get what you think you get, absolutely the Tonic of Nature's own providing, com- prised of the beneecient properties contained in Sar- saparilla, Saffron, Gentian. Burdock, Lavender, and Dandelion in addition to Quinine. It is not go much what you pay for a thing, but what you get for what you pay. Don't listen to the "Just as geed " argu- ment, there is no Tonic " Just as good "19 wilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, it stand 4 supreme. To prevent disappointment, above all things see that yen get the right article, with the name " Garilsm Evans "on Label, Stamp, and Bottle, without which none is genuine. Sold everywhere in bottles 2s. 9d. and 49. 6J. each, but should any diffienlty be experienced in procur- ing Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, it will be forwarded carriage free, for the above prices, by the Sole Proprie- tors The Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Company, i Llanollo, South Wale..</p>
