      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-11-14_WidnesExaminer_art0087" n="art0087">
        <head>SUGGESTED AMALGAMATION OF TWO COMMITTEES.</head>
        <p>SUGGESTED AMALGAMATION OF TWO COMMITTEES.</p>
        <p>COURCiller TINNION suggested that the time had come when the Electricity Committee and the Tramways Committee should be merged into one. (Hear, hear.) There must be a great deal of overlapping in the work of these two committees, and considering the very great amount of time many members of the Council had to give to committee work it would be a wise thing to have the matter he had suggested taken in hand. If in order Ihe would move a resolution •n the subject at the next meeting of the Council or at the first opportunity that presented itself. The MAYOR said it had been suggested that the matter should be mentioned to the two committees.</p>
        <p>Councillor TINNION : At any reite I give notice of my intention to move a resclutiva on the subject.</p>
        <p>ELECTION OF PRESIDING ALDERMEN.</p>
        <p>Oa the motion of Councillor SMETHITRST. seconded by Councillor ROGERS, tho following were elected the pre- siding Alderman for the ensuing year :—Whitseress Ward, Alderman Monks ; Bewley,Alderman Fairclough; Orford, Alderman Hutchinson ; St John's, Alderman Sutton ; Falifield, Alderman Heaton ; Howley,Alierioan</p>
        <p>THE FOOD THAT MAKES</p>
        <p>IT IS</p>
        <p>THE MAN.</p>
        <p>If the food eaten be lacking in the required proportion of flesh, bone, and brain nourishing elements, the individual will be stunted, anzmic, weak, nervous, listless, and mentally dull. If, on the other hand, " FORCE " be eaten (" FORCE" is extremely rich in flesh, bone, and brain making materials), the person will be of good height, well-nourished, strong, iron- nerved, energetic, and mentally bright. .</p>
        <p>"FORCE" prevents ill-health therefore saves money.</p>
