      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-11-14_WidnesExaminer_art0116" n="art0116">
        <head>ELEVEN YEARS OF AN/EMIA ! --- Swooned • after a Short Walk. -- Now She Walks Ten Miles Easily.</head>
        <p>ELEVEN YEARS OF AN/EMIA ! --- Swooned • after a Short Walk. -- Now She Walks Ten Miles Easily.</p>
        <p>Bile Beans cause the Difference.</p>
        <p>Ar semia is easily summed up. It mears bloodleseness. The blood is the life. If you've only half-supply of bleed, you've only half-supply ef life and energy. If you pant and get breathless by going upstairs, if your lips and gums are pale, if lou've got headache every other day, and if you feel to have" no strength to crawl," depend upon it you've got aenmis. " For eleven years 'suffered with anmonia,and had an awful time," says Miss Eilen Cooke, a domestic servant of Inwood' Cottages, Woburn Sands. " The weakness caused by an rnia led to other ill 3. All any colour went. I was weak, out of breath with the least exertion, and at times felt almost lifeless. Then I began to have acute indigestion. The pain after even light food was terrible. With the least exertion I had palpitation, which made me afraid of over-taxing myself in the least As far as I dared I continued to attend to my duties ; and the result was that I became utterly prostrated and had to remain lying down and perfectly quiet until I could recover. On one eccasion I set out to reach a place five minutes' walk filial'. but I was so very weak that I swooned before I got there and had to be taken home. For six weeks I was to weak to live on any- thing but milk load. My father. very strongly advised me to give Bile Beans a trial, and I consented Well, I bad not been taking the Beans. more than a few days before I felt that I was benefiting. my appe- tite improved day by day ; and the food was digested without giving me any trcuble such as I used to have. Thanks entirely for Chas. Forde'S Bile Beans,l am now thoroughly recovered. I have neither the sickly look nor feeling I had before, and my appetite is quite eat.is- factory. Arsamis, palpitation. and chronic indigestion are eompiete strangers to me, and I never experience the fagged ' feeling I used to do. Only the other day I walked ten miles ; and neither then nor since have I experienced the least discomfort or sign of wearinesel Miss Cooke's parents fully bore out her statements. More conclusive testimony to the wonderful powers of Chas. Forde's Bile Beans for Biliousness could not be de- sired. They have earned for themselves the enviable reputation of lacing the " World's Greatest Specific " for uremia in its worst forms, chronic indigestion, pal- pitation, ulcerated stomach, and debility ; while they are also unsurpassed for headache, dizz;ness. pains in the chest, side, and back, constipation, piles, colds, chills, rheumatism, liver and kidney disorders, female ailments, nausea, and fulness after meals. All chemists stock Bile Beans, or they may be obtaited post free from the Bilo Bean Manufacturing Co., Bed Cross-street, London, E.G.. for prices le lid or 2e 9d (23 9d box con- tains 3 times Is lid).</p>
