        <p>ASSOCIATION FOOTBALL WARRINGTON DISTRICT LEAGUE. FIRST DIVISION. OUGHTRINGToN PARK V WAIRINeToN " GUARDIAN," These teams met at Oughtrington Park on Saturday. The visitors made the journey with only nine men and were out- classed throughout. In the first half the home team scored fonr goals and in the concluding stages three, against the visitors one. Final : Oughtrington Park, seven goals ; Warrington " Guardian," one goal. SECOND DIvIsIoN. DAREsBURT AND MOORE V. WARRINGTON AIBIoN. Played at Moore on Saturday. The visitors wen the toss and during the first half played with the wind, but at half- time there was no score In th second half the home team soon began to press, and John Loekhart scored. The visitors now tried their best to equalize, but the backs played well and kept them out. Risley, for the home team, had very hard lines in not searing a second goal, his shot striking the upright. The visitors now worked very hard to get on even terms, but there was no further score, the home team thus I Winning an exciting game by one goal to ail.</p>
